# Enforce the Data-Quality Checkpoint as a CI Gate

## 1. Project Overview

This task implements an automated data-quality gate in the `fraud-detector` repository using Gitea Actions and Great Expectations.

The objective was to ensure that the data-quality checkpoint runs automatically during pull-request validation. If the checkpoint fails, the workflow must return a non-zero exit code and fail the CI job, preventing a pull request from passing its required data-quality check.

## 2. Task Objectives

- Integrate the existing `drift_check` checkpoint into the CI workflow.
- Execute the checkpoint automatically for pull requests targeting `main`.
- Make checkpoint failures block the workflow.
- Verify that valid data passes the checkpoint.
- Avoid configurations that suppress validation failures.

