## 8. Expected Failure Behaviour

When the checkpoint detects invalid data and exits with a non-zero status, the ordinary workflow step should fail. This causes the `data-quality` job to fail rather than allowing the validation error to be ignored.

The successful CI result confirms the clean-data path. A separate deliberately corrupted-data test should be performed if explicit evidence of the failure path is required.

